--        (the ENTIRE complex critical strip 0 < Re(s) < 1, the line Re(s) = 1, and Re(s) > 1!),
--        the Abel-summed complex Dirichlet series for L(chi, s) converges ABSOLUTELY in C!
--   2. `zeta.complex_power_integral` & `zeta.complex_euler_maclaurin_csummable`:
--        Exact complex integral int_a^b x^(-s) dx = (b^(1-s) - a^(1-s)) / (1 - s) for ALL s != 1,
--        and ABSOLUTE CONVERGENCE of the complex Euler-Maclaurin analytic continuation series
--          sum_{n>=1} (n^(-s) - int_n^{n+1} x^(-s) dx) = zeta(s) - 1/(s-1)
--        for EVERY complex s with Re(s) > 0 and s != 1!
